services/sanitizer-core/detect/words/german-names.txt
  Byte copy of services/sanitizer/data/german-names.txt: 183 common German
  given names and surnames, compiled for the project. Its header names "Faker
  de_DE locale, Statistisches Bundesamt frequency lists". 123 of the 183
  entries are entries of Faker 30.8.2 de_DE (MIT, see german-given-names.txt).
  For the other 60 (Kim, Sascha and 58 surnames) the stated Statistisches
  Bundesamt source is NOT VERIFIED (2026-11-02): no surname list of the
  Statistisches Bundesamt was found, and the given-name tables it publishes
  give another source: "Quelle: Gesellschaft für deutsche Sprache"
  (Statistisches Jahrbuch, tables 2.2.7 and 2.2.8,
  https://www.destatis.de/DE/Themen/Querschnitt/Jahrbuch/jb-bevoelkerung.pdf;
  press release of 2019,
  https://www.destatis.de/DE/Presse/Pressemitteilungen/2019/09/PD19_363_122.html).
  Each of the 60 is an entry of the upstream smashew/NameDatabases lists that
  name-corpus.txt below is built from (The Unlicense; checked against
  NamesDatabases/surnames/all.txt and "first names"/all.txt at that commit: 52
  as written, 8 transliterated or accent-folded: Böhm, Gröner, König, Krüger,
  Kühn, Möller, Schröder, Strauß), and 38 of them are also Faker 30.8.2 de_AT
  or de_CH entries (MIT). The file is unchanged (in a one-off measurement for
  T-1441 K-D, removing the 60 dropped LS2 surname coverage from 94 to 73 of
  200 and 12 in-repo logins).

